    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by the elite efficiency of **Trea Turner** (77.33), who remains the cornerstone of our strategy given the league\u2019s acute scarcity of stolen bases. With Dollander on the mound offering a slow delivery and a high xERA of 4.41, **Trea Turner** is positioned to maximize his speed-based value out of the leadoff spot. Close behind is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.93), whose profile is arguably the most intriguing of the day; despite batting 8th, his high dynamic platoon grade against a right-handed pitcher and the 100% stolen base opportunity presented by Rocker\u2019s delivery profile make him a mandatory start in our pursuit of category dominance. **Kyle Schwarber** (70.60) also presents a strong play, leveraging an excellent .394 xwOBA and the same favorable matchup against Dollander to solidify the top of our scoring board.\n\nWe are navigating several complex platoon dynamics, most notably with **Yordan Alvarez** (54.97) and **Junior Caminero** (55.41). **Yordan Alvarez** faces a difficult L/L matchup against Lodolo, which suppresses his ceiling, though his elite underlying data forces his inclusion. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** battles a 3.03 xERA arm in Early, but benefits significantly from wind conditions and an advantageous 3-hole spot. While the bench is largely cleared due to the unavailability of **Christian Yelich**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Colt Keith**, and the minor-league assignment of **Zac Veen**, the decision to bench other depth pieces was straightforward. The closest call for the final UTIL spot involved weighing the mid-tier consistency of **Dillon Dingler** (54.93) against our higher-variance bench options, but the optimizer prioritized **Dillon Dingler**'s favorable platoon edge against Bubic over alternatives who lacked a clear path to everyday at-bats. We remain cautious regarding **Kazuma Okamoto** (47.46) and **Caleb Durbin** (42.94), as both face difficult pitchers with xERAs near or below 3.15, rendering their starts marginal and dependent on potential park-factor wind assistance to maintain value.",
